{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Happy are you, O Israel — who is like you.</b> This verse is an explicit promise to Israel concerning the matter of the World to Come. For since he mentioned in the previous verse the bodily promises — namely, the blessing of the land and the abundance of tranquility and goodness, which is a land of grain and wine, and that His heavens above bring down dew for blessing, and that Israel shall dwell there in safety, fearing no foe or enemy, and that no nation shall dwell there but Israel alone — and this is what he said, 'in solitude' (בדד), in the manner of what is written (Numbers 23:9): הן עם לבדד ישכון — therefore he needed to add and explain, 'Happy are you, O Israel — who is like you' (אשריך ישראל מי כמוך). That is to say: do not think that this will be for you the ultimate recompense and the reward for the commandments. And therefore you will find difficulty in the word 'people' (עם), and its meaning is: who is like you — a people (עם) among the peoples — who will have both the bodily promises and the promises of the soul, and who will have goodness and tranquility in a good and spacious land in this world, and who will be saved (נושע) by HaShem, may He be exalted, for the life of the World to Come. And you already know that the true salvation is none other than for the World to Come; therefore it says, 'saved by HaShem' (נושע בה׳), which is like the language of (Isaiah 45:17): ישראל נושע בה׳ תשועת עולמים. And after he mentioned the reward of the World to Come, he gave them a sign for this: that the Holy One, blessed be He, will be their shield and their help and the sword of their pride, meaning that they will be able to take pride in it — this is what it says, מגן עזרך ('the shield of your help'). And it further includes that He calls the divine attribute of Judgment above a 'shield,' because the way of the shield is to be on the left side, and He promises us through it that it will be in our help and we shall not fear the enemy but prevail over him; and so David said (Psalms 18:36): ותתן לי מגן ישעך. And he further explained and said (Psalms 84:12): כי שמש ומגן ה׳ אלהים — he called the great Name 'sun' and the divine attribute of Judgment above 'shield,' and this is what it says here, מגן עזרך ('the shield of your help') ואשר חרב גאותך ('and who is the sword of your pride'). For when Israel has constant success and overwhelming victory over all their enemies — lo, this is for them a sign that they are cleaving to and saved by the Holy One, blessed be He, for the World to Come. And this is a great principle for all the promises in the Torah, such as those in the section אם בחקותי: the intention is not that those promises in this world are the ultimate reward for fulfillment of the commandments, but they are a sign for the people that they will merit the World to Come through the fulfillment of all their desire in this world. And it was fitting for the Torah, all whose words are peace and truth, to have the World to Come as its seal; and also for the king of Israel, the faithful servant who is prepared for the life of the World to Come — it was fitting that on the day he blessed the tribes of Israel and their assembly, he take his leave of them through words of the supernal, hidden world; and therefore he chose to seal his words with it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:54:35.665326109Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}